-- expect: 10:3: `yield` is in the body of a generator only, a `gen fn` or a `gen { … }` block; so is a call whose callback yields, which delegates to the generator it makes
-- A callback that yields makes the function that calls it a generator (`twice` is specialized
-- into one), and its call delegates to that generator: it yields to whoever runs the code around
-- it. `main` is not a generator; `for x in gen { twice(…) } { … }` runs it.
fn twice(f: !(i32 => 1), x: i32) -> 1 =
  f(x);
  f(x + 1)

main -> i32 =
  twice(!{ y -> yield y }, 5);
  0
